==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|la|rēctō}} {{m|la|folium|foliō|on the right leaf, on the right page}}, the [[Appendix:Glossary#ablative case|ablative case]] of the Latin {{m|la|rēctus||right}}. Confer {{m|la|versus||turned}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛk.toʊ/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Recto and verso}}
{{en-noun}}

# The front side of a flat object which is to be examined visually, as for reading, such as a sheet or a leaf or a [[coin]] or a [[medal]].
# Therefore, {{lb|en|printing}} the [[right-hand]] [[page]] of a [[book]] of a script which reads from left to right, usually having an odd page number.
# {{lb|en|legal}} A [[writ]] of [[right]].

